# A. M. Rubinov and I. Singer, "Topical and Sub-Topical Functions" (2001)

Bibliography label: Rubinov--Singer 2001.

Published source: A. M. Rubinov and I. Singer, *Topical and sub-topical
functions, downward sets and abstract convexity*, Optimization 50(5--6)
(2001), 307--351. DOI: `10.1080/02331930108844567`.

The paper calls a map topical when it is order-preserving and additively
homogeneous, and sub-topical when it is order-preserving and additively
subhomogeneous. This is the relevant established name for scalar max-affine
stopping maps `x ↦ max b (t + a*x)` with `0 ≤ a ≤ 1`: they are monotone and
satisfy `f (x + c) ≤ f x + c` for `c ≥ 0`.

This file is a source-positioning note. It states no Lean version of the
paper's abstract-convexity results.
